[sliver] Functional snap-hook catch faces and 45° entry bevels on the two 3 mm high hooks. Each catch face projects 0.85 mm: the required 0.6 mm engagement plus 0.25 mm running clearance. Its diagonal entry face is 1.202 mm wide. Those are the dimensions of the working catch profile, rather than 0.85 mm or 1.202 mm wall sections; the spring wings are 3 mm thick. The full 54.5 mm extrusion prints axially with no supports or interrupted wings.
alternatives: A 1.6 mm catch projection requires another 0.75 mm of spring deflection and deeper receiving pockets, changing the snap's assembly force and engagement. Removing the flats removes the catch bearing. Rounding the entry face still requires the flat retention bearing beneath it.
