[thin] The continuous working spring arch is nominally 2.4 mm between the 3 mm wings. Its exported minimum is 2.322 mm: the fitted motor bore follows the measured barrel axis while the outside profile stays straight. This is the named flexure, with three Classic loops and 100% solid infill in the actual support-free slice. The native fit clears the motor and mating lid; physical snap force and vibration life are not established by that reading.
alternatives: A 3 mm outer arch adds 0.6 mm above the present crown, exceeding the measured 0.311 mm PSU gap at this placement. Growing into the motor bore consumes its 0.15 mm static fit allowance. A thicker arch also changes the spring's stiffness; the selected working section retains the fitted motor envelope and available PSU room.
